1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:05,310
How do you measure
the slope of a curve?

2
00:00:05,360 --> 00:00:07,280
A point P on the curve y = x²

3
00:00:07,330 --> 00:00:09,550
A curve keeps bending,
so we can't measure its slope directly

4
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:11,720
So put another point Q next to it
and join the two with a straight line

5
00:00:11,770 --> 00:00:17,790
Slide Q closer and closer to P…

6
00:00:17,840 --> 00:00:19,760
The slope closes in on 2!

7
00:00:19,810 --> 00:00:22,130
When the two points become one = the tangent line
Its slope = 2

8
00:00:22,180 --> 00:00:26,600
Let's zoom way in on P

9
00:00:26,650 --> 00:00:31,970
The curve almost lies on the tangent —
up close, a curve looks straight!

10
00:00:32,020 --> 00:00:34,740
Finding this slope is "differentiation":
the slope seen from really close up

11
00:00:34,790 --> 00:00:41,710
Move P and the slope changes too

12
00:00:41,760 --> 00:00:45,210
The slope is always twice x
(x²)′ = 2x

13
00:00:46,210 --> 00:00:49,960
NEXT: Average 100 km/h means
exactly 100 at some moment?
